# Normalise everything to LF in the repository and on checkout. Contributors on
# Windows can still have `core.autocrlf=true` locally without it reaching a blob.
* text=auto eol=lf

# docs/reference/openapi.json is the ONE exception, and it is load-bearing.
#
# scripts/sync_catalog.py saves the served specification byte-for-byte verbatim,
# and the CDN serves it with CRLF line endings. scripts/check_drift.py then
# BYTE-COMPARES the committed copy against a fresh fetch, so any line-ending
# conversion — Git's on commit, or an editor's on save — breaks that comparison
# and turns the `drift` job red on a pull request that never touched the file.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions.
docs/reference/openapi.json -text

# Brand assets are byte-for-byte copies of the originals.
assets/*.svg -text
